From: Jason Walker <59085866+jaso1000@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:10:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] HD voice (AMR-WB), Soong build, Kotlin 2 fixes

AMR-WB (16 kHz) is offered first with AMR (8 kHz) as fallback; the codec the network picks (first
payload type in the answer / AMR-WB when offered in an incoming INVITE) sets the capture and
playback rate, the MediaCodec encoder/decoder, the speech mode (highest in the mode-set, default
12.65 kbit/s) and the telephone-event clock. Amr.kt packs and unpacks the RFC 4867
bandwidth-efficient payload for every AMR and AMR-WB mode (byte-identical to the old code for
AMR 12.2). Off switch: persist.fold3.ims.amrwb=false. Verified on Telstra: AMR-WB 12.65 outgoing
and incoming, AMR fallback, DTMF.

Android.bp: builds in a platform tree (RNNoise JNI lib in the APK, ImsMediaFramework.jar bundled
like the Gradle build, PhhImsOverlay not required). Kotlin 2: non-null assertion on
activeSubscriptionInfoList, final override for SipRequest.headers.

---
